			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Rebuild Target artifacts and update RouteManifest timestamp\n\nRecompile all ESBuild output bundles in `Target/` after the preceding Mountain gRPC integration and architecture-diagram refactor, synchronizing the compiled JS with the refreshed source.\n\nUpdate `Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts` generation timestamp from `2026-05-19T04:08:18Z` to `2026-05-19T04:25:35Z`. The 19 compiled target files (JS bundles + source maps across Bootstrap, Effect, gRPC, Service, and Handler layers) remain byte-identical in size, confirming no source-level changes occurred between rebuilds.\n\nThis keeps the build pipeline consistent and the manifest aligned with the latest compilation cycle.",
			"SHA": "7d8b9aaa73ff85751d7e0292f67d51d41bbc65d5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T04:20:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				1143,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Restructure architecture diagram and simplify Mountain notification wiring\n\nRedraw the README Mermaid diagram into semantically grouped subgraphs (Bootstrap, Effects, Services, Transport, Support) with labeled blocks, making the lifecycle and data flow between Cocoon's modules immediately readable. Replace the lost `classDef` for IPC and add a clear visual distinction between the gRPC transport layer and the Effect-TS orchestration layer.\n\nSimplify `Source/Services/Command.ts` by removing the dynamic import indirection — the `mountainClient` is already yielded from `IMountainClientService` at the service scope, so it can call `sendNotification` directly. This eliminates a redundant async import and potential race condition.\n\nRemove the Mountain extension scanner merge loop from `Source/Services/Extension.ts` and replace it with an explanatory comment. Loading extension metadata here without a valid `extensionLocation: VSCode.Uri` produced broken entries that cascaded into `path.join(undefined)` errors when VS Code resolved extension resources. The actual extension host receives extension data via `$deltaExtensions` gRPC, making this merge both incorrect and unnecessary.\n\nRebuild all `Target/` artifacts and update `RouteManifest.ts` generation timestamp to 2026-05-19T04:08:18Z.",
			"SHA": "7f56bdf6e9e5ab100279bfb061fa363aec67ea20"
		},
